      "side": 1,
      "message": "While less probable, I think the main issue being fixed can still happen on PID reuse. I\u0027m not sure how probable it is, though. Not a blocker, but if you wanted to make it bulletproof, maybe we could enforce a floor - at module level:\n\n```\n# Timestamp used for classifying core recency\n_START_TIMESTAMP \u003d time.time()\n```\n\nand here then:\n\n```    \nmatches \u003d [\n        m\n        for m in glob.glob(glob_pat)\n        if os.path.isfile(m) and os.path.getmtime(m) \u003e\u003d _START_TIMESTAMP - 1\n    ]\n```\n\nit doesn\u0027t matter if the timestamp is main or child - it still will be \u003c\u003d than any vpp core run by that particular child",
      "revId": "8d94988e44a814ef70cb39a6bcb1d5a40f5028c6",
